<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
launchd agent for Orion log rotation.

Why this exists: Orion's structured logs (orion.log, orion_errors.log,
orion_YYYY-MM-DD.log) are rotated by empire_core's RotatingFileHandler, but two
other classes of log are not rotated by anything:

  - wrapper redirects, e.g. run_execution_native.sh ends in
    `exec python -m orion.main_execution >> logs/execution_native.log`
  - launchd redirects, i.e. StandardOutPath / StandardErrorPath

Both are plain O_APPEND handles held for the life of the process, so they grow
without bound. On 2026-08-13 execution_native.log had reached 6.5 GB and the
logs dir 20 GB (a gateway-error storm accounted for most of it).

The script truncates in place rather than renaming — a running service holds an
open fd, and renaming would leave it writing to the renamed inode. It is
therefore safe to run against live services and needs no restart.

Schedule: 03:30 local, daily. Deliberately outside the 06:30-13:00 PT market
session so a multi-GB gzip never competes with ingestion for CPU.

Install (create the log dir FIRST — launchd opens StandardOutPath /
StandardErrorPath below before the script ever runs, so a missing logs/ dir
would stop the job launching at all, silently):
    mkdir -p /Users/jacobmcmillan/Empire/Orion/logs
    cp scripts/launchd/com.empire.orion.log-rotation.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.empire.orion.log-rotation.plist

Status / run once by hand:
    launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.empire.orion.log-rotation
    launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.empire.orion.log-rotation

Verify without changing anything:
    scripts/rotate_native_logs.sh --dry-run
    scripts/rotate_native_logs.sh --self-check
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.empire.orion.log-rotation</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/jacobmcmillan/Empire/Orion/scripts/rotate_native_logs.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/jacobmcmillan/Empire/Orion</string>

    <!-- Daily at 03:30 local: well clear of the cash session. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>3</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>

    <!-- A rotation pass is a one-shot; never keep it alive. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>

    <!-- Rotation output is one JSON line per action. These two files are
         themselves in the allowlist, so the job trims its own logs. -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/jacobmcmillan/Empire/Orion/logs/log_rotation.stdout.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/jacobmcmillan/Empire/Orion/logs/log_rotation.stderr.log</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/jacobmcmillan</string>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/opt/homebrew/bin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
